<% content_for :title, "Support · InternalQ" %>
<div class="kv-page">
  <div class="kv-page-header">
    <div class="kv-heading-group">
      <h1>Support</h1>
      <p class="kv-page-subtitle">What you can do, how to do it, and where to get help.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="kv-static-content">
    <section class="kv-static-section">
      <h2>What you can do</h2>
      <p>Use InternalQ to <strong>ask questions in plain English</strong> and get answers from your company docs. You can do this in this app (Q&A page) or in Slack by @mentioning the bot. Only documents uploaded by your org are used. Admins manage documents and Slack connection; everyone in the org can ask questions and view documents.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="kv-static-section">
      <h2>How to get started</h2>
      <p>1) <%= link_to "Create an account", new_user_registration_path %> (first user becomes admin). 2) Go to <strong>Integrations</strong> and connect your Slack workspace. 3) Go to <strong>Documents</strong> and upload PDFs or DOCX (handbooks, policies). 4) Use <strong>Q&A</strong> here or in Slack to ask questions.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="kv-static-section">
      <h2>Slack bot</h2>
      <p>You can talk to the InternalQ bot in two ways:</p>
      <ul class="kv-meta-text">
        <li><strong>Direct message</strong> – Open a DM with the InternalQ app and send a question as a normal message.</li>
        <li><strong>Channels</strong> – In any channel, @mention the InternalQ bot in your message to ask a question.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The bot answers using your org’s uploaded documents and only reads messages sent directly to it or where it is mentioned.</p>
      <p>If the bot doesn’t respond:</p>
      <ul class="kv-meta-text">
        <li>Confirm Slack is connected under Integrations.</li>
        <li>Check that at least one document is uploaded and processed.</li>
        <li>In channels, make sure you mentioned the bot directly in the message.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="kv-static-section">
      <h2>Get help</h2>
      <p>For issues, feature ideas, or questions: email us at <a href="mailto:abhishekverma.gju@gmail.com">abhishekverma.gju@gmail.com</a> or use your normal internal support channel. <%= link_to "Privacy policy", privacy_path %> · <%= link_to "Install app", installation_path %></p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <div class="kv-soft-divider"></div>
  <p class="kv-meta-text kv-meta-muted">
    <%= link_to "Install", installation_path %> · <%= link_to "Privacy", privacy_path %>
  </p>
</div>
